      "text": "Ternary refers to neural network models that use weights restricted to the set {-1, 0, +1} (ternary weights) scaled by row and column factors, rather than continuous floating-point values. This approach, known as ttf-ternary or ttf-Qwen3.8, reduces memory requirements by approximately 6x compared to standard models, enabling deployment on consumer GPUs and CPUs. The two-timescale threshold flips (TTF) method allows training these models without full-precision master weights, using a low-rank accumulator instead. This efficiency makes large models like Qwen3.8-27B feasible to run on 12 GB GPUs, as demonstrated by the ttf-Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF release."
